    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but the entropy thing is exactly what i mean—the \"disorder\" we see is just the way the data looks as it's being re-integrated into the system. it seems like we're just moving toward a state of higher order, which is why it feels like we're \"remembering\" a structured past instead of experiencing a chaotic future. if we assume the endpoint is already set and we're just tracing the path back, wouldn't the \"predictions\" (memories) follow a specific mathematical sequence? i need to know how to map these \"memory spikes\" to a timeline so i can figure out the next major event i'm going to recover.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
